    "sourceText": "Q4. A doctor is known for his commitment to providing the best possible care to his patients. He believes that staying up-to-date with the latest advancements in medical research is crucial for delivering optimum clinical care. The doctor frequently engages in a process that involves systematically reviewing, appraising, and using clinical research findings to guide his decisions and treatment plans. His colleagues often ask him about the name of this approach, which is considered a cornerstone of modern healthcare. The doctor explains that it is the very definition of a fundamental concept in healthcare.\nWhat is the definition that the Doctor is referring to? \nA. Computerized Physician Order Entry\nB. Electronic Medical Records \nC. Evidence Based Medicine\nD. Clinical Decision Support System\nAnswer:C",
